            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for a giant, then the Arabic for a dwarf."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: أهدى",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أهدى — ahdā — \"to gift; to dedicate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أهدت البنت وردة إلى أمها. ahdat al-bint wardatan ilā ummihā. The girl gave her mother a rose."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يهدي, yuhdī."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The taught هدية, a gift, is its noun. Of a book: أهدى (ahdā) الكتاب إلى أمه, he dedicated it to his mother."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أهدى (ahdā) is built on the native Arabic root h-d-y (Lane), \"to guide\", the root of the taught hadiyya, a gift. It is Form IV, \"to send a gift\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
